00:48:28,888 --> 00:48:34,888
Ant-Man and the Wasp is a 2018 American superhero film based on Marvel Comics
featuring the characters Scott Lang / Ant-Man and Hope Pym / Wasp.

12
00:52:53,333 --> 00:52:59,333
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures, it is the
sequel to Ant-Man (2015) and the 20th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
00:57:17,777 --> 00:57:23,777
The film was directed by Peyton Reed and written by the writing teams of Chris McKenna
and Erik Sommers, and Paul Rudd, Andrew Barrer and Gabriel Ferrari.

14
01:01:42,222 --> 01:01:48,222
It stars Rudd as Lang and Evangeline Lilly as Hope van Dyne, alongside Michael Peña, Walton Goggins, Hannah John-Kamen, David Dastmalchian, Tip
"T.I." Harris, Judy Greer, Bobby Cannavale, Randall Park, Abby Ryder Fortson, Michelle Pfeiffer, Laurence Fishburne, and Michael Douglas.

15
01:06:06,666 --> 01:06:12,666
In the film, the titular pair work with Hank Pym (Douglas) to
retrieve Janet van Dyne (Pfeiffer) from the Quantum Realm.

16
01:10:31,111 --> 01:10:37,111
Talks for a sequel to Ant-Man began shortly after that film was released.

17
01:14:55,555 --> 01:15:01,555
Ant-Man and the Wasp was officially announced in October 2015, with
Rudd and Lilly returning to reprise their roles.

18
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
A month later, Ant-Man director Reed was officially set to return.

19
01:23:44,444 --> 01:23:50,444
He had joined the first film later in its production and was
excited to develop this one from the beginning.

20
01:28:08,888 --> 01:28:14,888
He also looked forward to introducing Hope van Dyne as the Wasp in this
film, and insisted on treating Lang and her as equals.

21
01:32:33,333 --> 01:32:39,333
Filming took place from August to November 2017, at Pinewood Atlanta Studios in Fayette County,
Georgia, as well as Metro Atlanta; San Francisco; Savannah, Georgia; and Hawaii.

22
01:36:57,777 --> 01:37:03,777
Ant-Man and the Wasp had its world premiere in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on June 25, 2018, and was
released in the United States on July 6, 2018, as part of Phase Three of the MCU.

23
01:41:22,222 --> 01:41:28,222
The film was a critical and commercial success, receiving praise for its performances (particularly
those of Rudd and Lilly), humor, and levity, and grossing over $622 million worldwide.

24
01:45:46,666 --> 01:45:52,666
A sequel, Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania, was released in February 2023.

25
